Evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

initial_response:
To evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when c=3, we simply substitute c=3 into the expression and simplify:
\begin{align*}
\left(3^3-3(3-1)^3\right)^3&=\left(27-3(2)^3\right)^3\\
&=\left(27-3\cdot 8\right)^3\\
&=(27-24)^3\\
&=(3)^3\\
&=27
\end{align*}

critique:
The assistant made a computation error in the expression \begin{align*}
3(2)^3=3\cdot8=24
\end{align*} should be \begin{align*}
3(2)^3=3\cdot2^3=3\cdot8=24
\end{align*}, and then correctly computed the rest of the expression.

revised_response:
To evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when c=3, we substitute c=3 into the expression and simplify:
\begin{align*}
\left(3^3-3(3-1)^3\right)^3&=\left(3^3-3(2)^3\right)^3\\
&=\left(27-3\cdot 8\right)^3\\
&=(27-24)^3\\
&=(3)^3
\end{align*}

Since \begin{align*}
3^3=27
\end{align*}, the result of the original expression is 27.

