revised_response:
The correct equation is $ \frac35 \cdot \frac19 \cdot x = 6$, where the left-hand side must have the same units as the right-hand side.

To solve for $x$, multiply both sides by the reciprocal of the product of the fractions:
\begin{align*}
\frac{3}{5} \cdot \frac{1}{9} \cdot x &= 6\\
\Rightarrow\qquad x &= 6 \cdot \frac{5}{3} \cdot \frac{9}{1}\\
&= 6 \cdot \frac{5 \cdot 3}{1}\\
&= 6 \cdot 15\\
&= \boxed{90 \text{ units}}
\end{align*}

where the result, 90 units, is dimensionless, as expected in this problem context.

