revised_response:
Since $\overline{BC}$, $\overline{DE}$ and $\overline{FG}$ are all parallel to $\overline{HI}$ and $AB = BD = DF = FH$, we can conclude that $\overline{AG}$ is parallel to $\overline{BC}$, $\overline{FG}$ and $\overline{HI}$. Also, since $\triangle HIG$ and $\triangle BGC$ are congruent, we have $[HIG]=[BCG]$. Since $AB=BD$, we know that $\overline{AB}$ is parallel to $\overline{CD}$ and $\overline{FG}$ is parallel to $\overline{HI}$. Therefore, $[AGI]=[FGI]$. We can then simplify the ratio of areas as \begin{align*}
\frac{[FGH]}{[AHI]}&=\frac{[FGH]+[HIG]-[AGI]}{[AHI]}\\
&=\frac{[FGH]+[BCG]-[BHD]}{[AHI]}\\
&=\frac{[AHI]-[BHD]}{[AHI]}=\frac12.
\end{align*}

