\|\mathbf{a}\|^2 + 2\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} + \|\mathbf{b}\|^2 &= \| \mathbf{a} \|^2 \\
2\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} + \|\mathbf{b}\|^2 &= 0 \\
\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} &= -\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{b}\|^2
\end{align*}
We then recall the definition of the dot product, $\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} = \|\mathbf{a}\|\|\mathbf{b}\|\cos \theta,$ where $\theta$ is the angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}.$
\begin{align*}
\|\mathbf{a}\|\|\mathbf{b}\|\cos \theta &= -\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{b}\|^2 \\
