To find $(\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1},$ we know that $(\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1} = (\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2.$ So, to find $(\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2,$ we can square $\mathbf{A}^{-1}$:
\begin{align*}
\left(\begin{pmatrix} -4 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix}\right)^2 &= \left(\begin{pmatrix} (-4)^2 + 0 & (-4)(1) + 2 \\ 0 & 2^2 \end{pmatrix}\right) \\
